<article class="env-lemma" id="0H6D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H6D">Lemma <span data-tag="0H6D">62.13.1</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Section <a href="/tag/0H65" data-tag="0H65">62.12</a>. Let $f : X' \to X$ be a proper morphism of schemes locally of finite type over $S$. Let $(\mathcal{L}, s, i : D \to X)$ be as in Chow Homology, Definition <a href="/tag/02T8" data-tag="02T8">42.29.1</a>. Form the diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ D' \ar[d]_ g \ar[r]_{i'} &  X' \ar[d]^ f \\  D \ar[r]^ i &  X }  \]
</div>
  <p> as in Chow Homology, Remark <a href="/tag/0B6Y" data-tag="0B6Y">42.29.7</a>. If $\mathcal{L}|_ D \cong \mathcal{O}_ D$, then $i^*f_*\alpha ' = g_*(i')^*\alpha '$ in $Z_ k(D)$ for any $\alpha ' \in Z_{k + 1}(X')$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The statement makes sense as all operations are defined on the level of cycles, see Chow Homology, Remark <a href="/tag/0B6Z" data-tag="0B6Z">42.29.6</a> for the Gysin maps. Suppose $\alpha = [W']$ for some integral closed subscheme $W' \subset X'$. Let $W = f(W') \subset X$. In case $W' \not\subset D'$, then $W \not\subset D$ and we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  [W' \cap D']_ k = \text{div}_{\mathcal{L}'|_{W'}}({s'|_{W'}}) \quad \text{and}\quad [W \cap D]_ k = \text{div}_{\mathcal{L}|_ W}(s|_ W)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       and hence $f_*$ of the first cycle equals the second cycle by Chow Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02ST" data-tag="02ST">42.26.3</a>. Hence the equality holds as cycles. In case $W' \subset D'$, then $W \subset D$ and both sides are zero by construction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>